cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Railway Wagon Stitching Benchmark
message: >-
  If you use this evaluation framework or the benchmark dataset,
  please cite the associated paper.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-17
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/AlejandroDiazD/railway-stitching-benchmark
url: https://github.com/AlejandroDiazD/railway-stitching-benchmark
abstract: >-
  Three-tier evaluation framework and benchmark protocol for sequential
  image stitching of railway wagons seen by a fixed trackside camera.
  Scores a stitching system from its reported frame offsets alone,
  combining Degenerate Rate, Displacement Accuracy and Sequence Stability
  into a weighted geometric mean. The companion dataset of 30 wagon
  sequences with 262 manually annotated frame pairs is available on
  request.
keywords:
  - image stitching
  - railway inspection
  - evaluation framework
  - benchmark dataset
  - industrial computer vision
